From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:25:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cix: scope ACPI property reference child-name strings to Sky1

Patch 3002 made acpi_get_ref_args() treat every ACPI_TYPE_STRING element
immediately following a device reference as a child data node name and
return -EINVAL on lookup failure. Standard ACPI _DSD reference packages
also allow a string element to start the next reference in the package,
so unconditionally consuming following strings breaks valid ACPI string
references on non-Sky1 platforms and whenever a string begins the next
reference.

Gate the child-name string walk on cix_sky1_acpi() and stop the walk
without clobbering ref_fwnode or advancing *element when
acpi_fwnode_get_named_child_node() returns NULL so non-Sky1 systems keep
mainline ACPI string-reference parsing and Sky1 falls through cleanly to
parse a following string-form reference.

Signed-off-by: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/acpi/property.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/property.c b/drivers/acpi/property.c
index f03c533..8b84a9b 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/property.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/property.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/export.h>
+#include <linux/soc/cix/sky1.h>
 
 #include "internal.h"
 
@@ -874,19 +875,26 @@ static int acpi_get_ref_args(struct fwnode_reference_args *args,
 		num_args = acpi_fwnode_get_args_count(ref_fwnode, nargs_prop);
 
 	/*
-	 * Consume consecutive string elements as hierarchical _DSD data node
-	 * path components.  ACPI graph references encode the path to a remote
-	 * endpoint as: Package { DEV, "port@N", "endpoint@N" }
-	 * Each string names a child data node under the preceding reference.
+	 * On CIX Sky1 ACPI firmware, graph references encode the path to a
+	 * remote endpoint as: Package { DEV, "port@N", "endpoint@N" }.
+	 * Consume consecutive string elements only when they name a child
+	 * data node under the preceding reference; otherwise stop so a
+	 * string-form reference starting the next entry is parsed normally.
 	 */
-	for (; *element < end && (*element)->type == ACPI_TYPE_STRING;
-	     (*element)++) {
-		const char *child_name = (*element)->string.pointer;
+	if (*element < end && (*element)->type == ACPI_TYPE_STRING &&
+	    cix_sky1_acpi()) {
+		for (; *element < end && (*element)->type == ACPI_TYPE_STRING;
+		     (*element)++) {
+			const char *child_name = (*element)->string.pointer;
+			struct fwnode_handle *child;
+
+			child = acpi_fwnode_get_named_child_node(ref_fwnode,
+								 child_name);
+			if (!child)
+				break;
 
-		ref_fwnode = acpi_fwnode_get_named_child_node(ref_fwnode,
-							      child_name);
-		if (!ref_fwnode)
-			return -EINVAL;
+			ref_fwnode = child;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/*
